## Repairs and partner credits

If CarmaCars turns it on for you, **Money** > **Statements** also shows the repair costs and partner credits on your own cars this year, with who paid each repair. It is not part of your statements or payouts.

## Statement periods and price limits (release 35)

- Each statement covers the 8th of one month to the 7th of the next, and the payout on the 10th pays it. A rental across the cutoff is paid for the days in each period, never twice.
- Amounts a renter still owes are listed apart on your statement and paid on the statement after we collect them.
- Set the lowest and highest daily rate for every car or one car: short-notice pricing, promo codes, discounts and our offers stay between them.

## Your forecast (release 48)

**Home** has a **Forecast** section: the next 12 months of each of your cars, with its projected occupancy and projected owner revenue (before fees). Open a car to see its months; with several cars, the line on top adds them up.

- Every car starts from the GTA''s rental season: January and February are quiet, March Break and the long weekends pick up, July and August are the busiest, and December brings holiday travel.
- Once a car has 3 full months on the program, its own occupancy is blended in, and it counts for more each month: half after 3 months, two thirds after 6, four fifths after 12. Under each car you see how its forecast is made.
- Projected owner revenue uses your car''s own statements of the last 12 months, per day booked; a newer car uses its daily rate less the Revenue Share.
- Bookings hidden from you are never counted.

Each statement also has a **Forecast** line: whether next month is projected higher or lower than the statement''s month, by how many points of occupancy and about how much owner revenue, and why (the season).

> Note: A forecast is an estimate, not a promise. Your statements and payouts are always what your car actually earned.',
